      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To examine the thoughts and concerns of men contemplating vasectomy before speaking to a physician as well as their partner's role in reaching this decision."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "A questionnaire analysis using response rates, ANOVA, and regression analyses."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "A large Midwestern teaching hospital."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENT(S)",
          "content": "Visitors to the urology clinic of the hospital."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTION(S)",
          "content": "None."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE(S)",
          "content": "[1] Questionnaire designed by authors. [2] Measures of self-concept, relationship satisfaction, and problem-solving abilities."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULT(S)",
          "content": "[1] Subjects had been considering vasectomy for an average of 1 year and were fairly certain of their decision. [2] Anxiety about vasectomy surgery was mostly driven by fear about pain and fear of the unknown. [3] Concerns about the finality of the procedure did not emerge as a big concern. [4] There is confusion about the reversibility of the procedure. [5] Subjects are better problem solvers and have a higher self-concept than people in general."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION(S)",
          "content": "Our findings demonstrate the need for adequate prevasectomy counseling, particularly in the area of postoperative expectations, as well as reversibility of the procedure."
        }
      ]},
